    <article><h3>Lived experience</h3><p>Real-world frustration keeps the company focused on solutions people can actually prepare, understand and use.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Health care</h3><p>Clinical experience keeps safety, patient context and the limits of generalized advice visible.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Nutrition science</h3><p>Physiology and ingredient rationale are separated from slogans so mechanisms can be explained without overclaiming.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Performance</h3><p>Athlete and coaching contexts test whether hydration plans remain practical when heat, sweat, travel and competition complicate the day.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

